1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:01,789
Hey friends, long time no see!

2
00:00:01,789 --> 00:00:04,599
This is episode zero of our 'Build in Public' series.

3
00:00:05,070 --> 00:00:06,701
I'll be regularly updating this channel

4
00:00:06,701 --> 00:00:08,458
with my AI product's development progress,

5
00:00:08,458 --> 00:00:09,630
and we'll build it together.

6
00:00:10,010 --> 00:00:11,435
I'll also share thoughts and experiences

7
00:00:11,435 --> 00:00:12,290
from my startup journey.

8
00:00:12,530 --> 00:00:13,212
Our product, Cora,

9
00:00:13,212 --> 00:00:15,261
has gone through two rounds of internal testing,

10
00:00:15,261 --> 00:00:17,037
and its form has changed quite a bit—more

11
00:00:17,037 --> 00:00:18,250
on that in the next episode.

12
00:00:18,730 --> 00:00:22,050
Today, I'm sharing a feature demo from our latest MVP round.

13
00:00:22,570 --> 00:00:25,190
Cora is a completely free browser plugin

14
00:00:25,190 --> 00:00:27,091
that solves just one problem:

15
00:00:27,091 --> 00:00:29,022
context transfer for creators

16
00:00:29,022 --> 00:00:31,220
between different creative tools.

17
00:00:31,580 --> 00:00:33,420
You can use it with Feishu, Jee, Meng,

18
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:36,082
Lovart, Tapnow, and more—dragging prompts,

19
00:00:36,082 --> 00:00:38,363
skills, characters, images, canvases, nodes,

20
00:00:38,363 --> 00:00:39,605
and even video assets

21
00:00:39,605 --> 00:00:41,527
to sync them with a single click

22
00:00:41,527 --> 00:00:43,510
to both local and external pages.

23
00:00:43,990 --> 00:00:45,753
So, during our previous Cora beta test,

24
00:00:45,753 --> 00:00:48,612
we found that AI native creators share a common pain point:

25
00:00:48,612 --> 00:00:50,709
their creative workflows are incredibly long.

26
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:51,795
And for each stage,

27
00:00:51,795 --> 00:00:53,520
there are different tools to boost efficiency.

28
00:00:53,880 --> 00:00:56,987
But the context between each stage—like prompts, asset images,

29
00:00:56,987 --> 00:00:59,784
storyboards, and so on—is scattered all over the place,

30
00:00:59,784 --> 00:01:01,960
making syncing a real headache every time.

31
00:01:02,550 --> 00:01:05,161
The essence of creation is aligning context,

32
00:01:05,161 --> 00:01:06,948
and the more fragmented it is,

33
00:01:06,948 --> 00:01:09,230
the harder it is to align—hence, Cora.

34
00:01:09,810 --> 00:01:11,258
In the next minute, I'll walk you

35
00:01:11,258 --> 00:01:13,249
through a simple example of how to use Cora.

36
00:01:13,610 --> 00:01:15,539
On Creaibo's website, download Cora,

37
00:01:15,539 --> 00:01:17,799
then follow the installation instructions.

38
00:01:18,060 --> 00:01:18,573
Once that's done,

39
00:01:18,573 --> 00:01:20,146
click on the plugin list in the top right corner,

40
00:01:20,146 --> 00:01:20,820
and then select Cora.

41
00:01:21,060 --> 00:01:22,420
Okay, if the plugin doesn't trigger,

42
00:01:22,420 --> 00:01:24,180
don't worry—just try refreshing the webpage

43
00:01:24,180 --> 00:01:25,260
or restarting your browser.

44
00:01:25,830 --> 00:01:27,990
So now, let me share my workflow with you all.

45
00:01:28,190 --> 00:01:29,855
For example, I jot down my stories in Notion,

46
00:01:29,855 --> 00:01:31,560
and once I capture them here with one click,

47
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:33,013
I can drag them straight into Creaibo

48
00:01:33,013 --> 00:01:34,350
to co create with my Claude Agent.

49
00:01:34,480 --> 00:01:36,426
So, once I've finished up the storyboards, scripts,

50
00:01:36,426 --> 00:01:37,805
images, videos, and prompts in Cora,

51
00:01:37,805 --> 00:01:39,206
I'll drop them into my Feishu docs

52
00:01:39,206 --> 00:01:40,360
for easy team collaboration.

53
00:01:42,410 --> 00:01:43,835
Once that's set up, I'll hop over to Lovart

54
00:01:43,835 --> 00:01:45,770
and use my prompts to generate all sorts of asset images.

55
00:01:46,050 --> 00:01:47,320
At this point, with Cora,

56
00:01:47,320 --> 00:01:50,580
you can just drag and drop to sync it right back to Feishu.

57
00:01:50,580 --> 00:01:51,252
Once it's finalized,

58
00:01:51,252 --> 00:01:53,376
we then take the storyboards, prompts, character asset images,

59
00:01:53,376 --> 00:01:54,297
and so on already in Cora,

60
00:01:54,297 --> 00:01:54,943
and with one click,

61
00:01:54,943 --> 00:01:56,740
pipe them over to Tapnow for automatic generation.

62
00:01:56,820 --> 00:01:58,819
So, we can see this node has finished running. From here,

63
00:01:58,819 --> 00:02:00,091
I'll go on to generate still frames

64
00:02:00,091 --> 00:02:01,218
and the subsequent video clips.

65
00:02:03,070 --> 00:02:04,211
But we're not done yet!

66
00:02:04,211 --> 00:02:07,064
Good content isn't just about piecing assets together,

67
00:02:07,064 --> 00:02:09,709
so I'll download them to CapCut for post production.

68
00:02:09,960 --> 00:02:11,181
So right now, I can just one click

69
00:02:11,181 --> 00:02:12,920
download the clips I just picked out in Tapnow.

70
00:02:14,310 --> 00:02:16,430
Let's import into CapCut.

71
00:02:17,030 --> 00:02:18,531
And I should also mention, in the future,

72
00:02:18,531 --> 00:02:20,211
we'll integrate with local editing software

73
00:02:20,211 --> 00:02:21,150
for asset preprocessing.

74
00:02:21,340 --> 00:02:23,238
Now, this case just shows my own workflow,

75
00:02:23,238 --> 00:02:25,660
but feel free to tweak it based on your own habits.

76
00:02:25,860 --> 00:02:28,293
For instance, Cora already supports most AI creation tools,

77
00:02:28,293 --> 00:02:29,660
with more to come in the future.

78
00:02:29,940 --> 00:02:31,900
In future versions, all these transferred assets

79
00:02:31,900 --> 00:02:34,069
will be automatically stored locally on your device

80
00:02:34,069 --> 00:02:35,000
and managed—classified,

81
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:36,780
organized, and sorted—by the Creaibo agent.

82
00:02:37,070 --> 00:02:39,220
The beta version is officially released.

83
00:02:39,220 --> 00:02:41,316
You can install it from creaibo dot com

84
00:02:41,316 --> 00:02:43,950
or by searching 'Cora' in your browser's app store.

85
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:46,178
So, Cora is just our new feature validation;

86
00:02:46,178 --> 00:02:47,788
our ultimate goal is still to solve

87
00:02:47,788 --> 00:02:49,122
the context handover problem

88
00:02:49,122 --> 00:02:50,640
in AI powered creative scenarios.

89
00:02:50,930 --> 00:02:53,330
making AI asset management more agentic.

90
00:02:53,490 --> 00:02:56,090
Any questions or suggestions? Feel free to comment below.

91
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:57,450
We're also actively hiring,

92
00:02:57,450 --> 00:02:58,928
so if you're into creation and love AI,

93
00:02:58,928 --> 00:02:59,637
feel free to apply

94
00:02:59,637 --> 00:03:01,878
and join us—check out our previous posts for the details

95
00:03:01,878 --> 00:03:02,159
on how.

